# Azure ↔ AWS Site-to-Site VPN Documentation

# Objective

Establish secure private communication between:

* Azure Virtual Network (VNet)
* AWS Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)

using:

* IPSec VPN Tunnel
* Azure VPN Gateway
* AWS Virtual Private Gateway

Goal:

* Azure Private VM should communicate with AWS Private EC2 using private IP addresses.
* No public IP exposure for workloads.
* Secure encrypted communication over the internet.

---

# Final Architecture

```text
Azure VNet (10.0.0.0/16)
│
├── Azure VM (10.0.1.4)
│
├── Azure VPN Gateway
│      Public IP: 4.187.241.207
│
└──────────── IPSec VPN Tunnel ────────────┐
                                           │
                                           │
AWS Virtual Private Gateway (VGW)
│
├── AWS VPC (172.16.0.0/16)
│
└── AWS EC2 Instance (172.16.0.130)
```

---

# Networking Concepts Used

| Concept                 | Purpose                            |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| VNet/VPC                | Private network in cloud           |
| Subnet                  | Smaller network inside VNet/VPC    |
| VPN Gateway             | Creates encrypted tunnel           |
| IPSec                   | Encrypts traffic                   |
| IKE                     | Negotiates VPN connection          |
| Diffie-Hellman          | Securely generates shared secret   |
| Route Table             | Decides traffic path               |
| NSG/Security Group      | Firewall rules                     |
| Local Network Gateway   | Represents remote network in Azure |
| Virtual Private Gateway | AWS VPN endpoint                   |

